Text: Why Decoder is Easier and More Sensitive The decoder in NMT model typically acts as a conditional language model, which generates to- kens highly depending on the previous tokens, like the standard language model (Khandelwal et al., 2018). We guess the conditional information (es- pecially the tokens right before the predicted to- ken) is too strong for the decoder. Therefore, we study the impact of the previous tokens as follows.

